WEBVTT

00:00:04.938 --> 00:00:07.607
As time moves on...

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:09.905
...nothing can return to what it was.

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:14.047
Once events begin to unfold...

00:00:14.047 --> 00:00:16.683
...all of the things, the soul...

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:18.048
...and the world itself...

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:21.688
...cannot change
course quickly...

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:24.624
...once they begin to move
in a particular direction.

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:26.393
Eventually...

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:29.089
...nobody will be able to
stop those events.

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:33.858
Is that girl really going to
make it in time?

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:37.670
Is she really going to be able
to do it?

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:06.663
I'd love to see "East Side Story"
and "The Princess and I."

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:09.798
You've got your duties.

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:11.971
That's enough
sightseeing.

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:12.938
What?

00:01:13.006 --> 00:01:15.041
You're the one who
dragged me out here.

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:18.111
I dropped everything and came
here without telling anyone...

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:21.376
...so I bet Tokio must be
pretty mad.

00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:24.751
Sorry about that.

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:28.521
Just when the TI psychic for the
U.S. is not able to function...

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:31.191
...we detected a pre-Raaja
reaction in Manhattan.

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:33.359
Uh, well, it's all right.

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:35.595
I did get a free trip to New York,
after all.

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:37.529
I feel I'm getting a good deal.

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:48.635
It's coming!

00:01:56.349 --> 00:02:02.447
Earth Maiden Arjuna

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:07.225
Episode 11: The Day of No Return

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:26.270
Hey, is your father alright?

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:28.073
Who knows?

00:02:28.515 --> 00:02:31.678
He's being interrogated daily.

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:36.654
But what can you do?

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:44.430
He was doing some
dangerous research...

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.955
...using a type of bacteria that can
decompose petroleum, after all.

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:49.669
Thanks to that...

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:52.605
...my mom's been coming
around everyday.

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:54.072
It must be hard on her.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:59.012
But more importantly...

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:01.742
...do you know where
Juna went?

00:03:02.515 --> 00:03:04.851
TI-2 Earth resonance
frequency detected.

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:06.419
- It's rapidly approaching
the Raaja reaction!

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:07.249
- Right!
- It's rapidly approaching
the Raaja reaction!

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:10.450
What a strong reaction.

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:34.038
Switch!

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:49.329
TI-2 sound reaction detected.

00:03:49.329 --> 00:03:51.097
One, the body effortlessly...

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:52.232
- That's too fast.
...permeates through all of the universe.

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:53.566
...permeates through all of the universe.

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:56.967
It's approaching the UN Building
at ten o'clock.

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:13.219
Two...

00:04:13.219 --> 00:04:18.486
...compose oneself,
and exhale onto Earth.

00:04:22.729 --> 00:04:23.630
Three...

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:26.199
...Iook far...

00:04:26.199 --> 00:04:28.394
...far beyond the limitless.

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:31.838
Four...

00:04:31.838 --> 00:04:33.973
...it is not the goal to
shoot the target...

00:04:33.973 --> 00:04:36.342
...but rather to become one...

00:04:36.342 --> 00:04:37.604
...with the target.

00:04:57.297 --> 00:04:58.423
You're late.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:48.214
Boy... where did Juna go
without telling anyone?

00:05:48.214 --> 00:05:51.351
Hey, you want to come
to my place tonight?

00:05:51.351 --> 00:05:52.251
Huh?

00:05:52.251 --> 00:05:55.154
I bet you haven't had
anything proper to eat lately.

00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:58.089
I'll make you a good
home-cooked meal.

00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:00.457
Are you sure?

00:06:01.728 --> 00:06:02.524
Sure.

00:06:04.097 --> 00:06:05.928
Now, come on. Step right in.

00:06:06.632 --> 00:06:08.623
Thank you.

00:06:15.074 --> 00:06:18.611
Um, I thought you were...

00:06:18.611 --> 00:06:21.681
...the type who'd live in
a place that would be...

00:06:21.681 --> 00:06:24.081
...featured in a
home decor magazine.

00:06:24.851 --> 00:06:27.086
One of those places that
looks inhuman?

00:06:27.086 --> 00:06:28.187
Yeah.

00:06:28.187 --> 00:06:30.314
Well, I mean, uh...

00:06:31.557 --> 00:06:34.583
Just make yourself some room
over there and have a seat.

00:06:34.794 --> 00:06:37.126
Make some room?

00:07:18.604 --> 00:07:19.798
Seems unlike me, right?

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:21.839
Uh, I was...

00:07:22.041 --> 00:07:23.269
It's all right.

00:07:23.743 --> 00:07:25.178
Once you see my room...

00:07:25.178 --> 00:07:28.511
...there's nothing else that can
embarrass me.

00:07:28.815 --> 00:07:29.975
Uh, thanks.

00:07:41.894 --> 00:07:44.192
Look at me laughing there
like a fool.

00:07:44.897 --> 00:07:48.901
This is from before
I joined S.E.E.D...

00:07:48.901 --> 00:07:51.631
...when I was part of the
environmental movement.

00:07:51.871 --> 00:07:54.574
We protested clear-cut logging...

00:07:54.574 --> 00:07:57.065
...and tried to close down
factories causing pollution.

00:07:58.711 --> 00:08:00.580
How foolish we were.

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:02.982
We thought the world
would change...

00:08:02.982 --> 00:08:05.109
...if we were against these things.

00:08:13.359 --> 00:08:14.849
You must have liked him.

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:20.089
Uh, I'm sorry.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:22.126
It's all history.

00:08:22.935 --> 00:08:25.404
We were quite the duo, you know.

00:08:25.404 --> 00:08:28.741
If only Kevin didn't tell me
he loved me.

00:08:28.741 --> 00:08:29.275
Huh?

00:08:29.275 --> 00:08:30.173
But...

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:34.170
There are some things that
can't be dealt with through love.

00:08:34.413 --> 00:08:35.311
But still...

00:08:40.853 --> 00:08:42.688
I'm not a woman.

00:08:42.688 --> 00:08:43.211
Huh?

00:08:43.556 --> 00:08:45.424
I'm actually a man.

00:08:45.424 --> 00:08:46.482
A man?

00:08:47.059 --> 00:08:49.254
Yes, I'm a man.

00:08:55.868 --> 00:08:57.103
Uh, um...

00:08:57.103 --> 00:08:59.435
...did you have a sex-change?

00:09:00.072 --> 00:09:01.507
No. That's not it.

00:09:01.507 --> 00:09:02.132
Look.

00:09:02.308 --> 00:09:04.276
This was when I was a child.

00:09:05.678 --> 00:09:07.113
I was so happy back then.

00:09:07.113 --> 00:09:10.616
I was able to live without
knowing who or what I was.

00:09:10.616 --> 00:09:13.085
But even after I started high school...

00:09:13.085 --> 00:09:16.543
...the changes you'd expect
in a young girl didn't happen.

00:09:16.722 --> 00:09:18.324
When I looked into it...

00:09:18.324 --> 00:09:21.691
...I turned out to be a hermaphrodite
possessing a Y chromosome.

00:09:21.994 --> 00:09:24.462
Biologically,
that made me a male.

00:09:25.798 --> 00:09:26.765
No way.

00:09:45.151 --> 00:09:48.348
Mr. Onizuka,
thank you for waiting.

00:09:48.688 --> 00:09:49.746
Well.

00:09:52.758 --> 00:09:54.385
l-lt's so tight...

00:09:55.761 --> 00:09:57.363
Thanks to the effects of hormones...

00:09:57.363 --> 00:09:59.888
...my mother's gametocyte
cells were all messed up.

00:10:01.167 --> 00:10:04.370
I'm sure my mom didn't realize
that the medicine...

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:07.703
...she took while pregnant
would have a side effect like that.

00:10:08.207 --> 00:10:09.141
But still...

00:10:09.141 --> 00:10:11.711
...I can't accept that you're...

00:10:11.711 --> 00:10:13.838
...anything other than a woman.

00:10:15.615 --> 00:10:17.480
You can't accept it, huh?

00:10:17.817 --> 00:10:19.512
That's why I got myself tested.

00:10:24.223 --> 00:10:25.758
Do you know why...

00:10:25.758 --> 00:10:29.819
...so many different drugs
are being manufactured?

00:10:30.029 --> 00:10:30.518
Huh?

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:32.290
Drugs?

00:10:32.798 --> 00:10:35.289
I have no idea...

00:10:36.235 --> 00:10:37.327
It's because of...

00:10:38.204 --> 00:10:39.228
...garbage.

00:10:41.374 --> 00:10:45.470
Earth Maiden Arjuna

00:10:47.513 --> 00:10:48.414
Of course...

00:10:48.414 --> 00:10:51.450
...there was medicine from long ago.

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:54.987
But the manufacturing of
chemical pharmaceuticals...

00:10:54.987 --> 00:10:57.649
...is the result of garbage,
or rather, industrial waste.

00:10:59.692 --> 00:11:02.795
You do know that they started
to mass produce...

00:11:02.795 --> 00:11:05.730
...all sorts of chemicals during
the Industrial Revolution, right?

00:11:05.931 --> 00:11:08.734
This led to a lot of coal, tar...

00:11:08.734 --> 00:11:10.836
...and other sorts of industrial waste.

00:11:10.836 --> 00:11:14.507
While they were finding ways
to process this material...

00:11:14.507 --> 00:11:17.908
...scientists discovered ways to
re-use the material as medicine.

00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:19.600
But, medicine is...

00:11:19.945 --> 00:11:22.114
Of course,
thanks to pharmaceuticals...

00:11:22.114 --> 00:11:24.283
...we've been able to
prevent infectious diseases...

00:11:24.283 --> 00:11:26.552
...and they've been useful
as pain killers.

00:11:26.552 --> 00:11:31.157
But there really aren't that many
illnesses that require medicine.

00:11:31.157 --> 00:11:31.891
In fact...

00:11:31.891 --> 00:11:33.325
...there's even a theory that...

00:11:33.325 --> 00:11:36.162
...a cold can function
to cleanse the body...

00:11:36.162 --> 00:11:37.686
...and make you tougher.

00:11:38.164 --> 00:11:39.529
Cleanse the body?

00:11:44.804 --> 00:11:46.572
If you take too much medicine...

00:11:46.572 --> 00:11:49.268
...toxins will build up in your body.

00:11:50.109 --> 00:11:51.577
It's not just medicine, either.

00:11:51.577 --> 00:11:52.043
Huh?

00:11:52.778 --> 00:11:55.948
During the First and Second
World Wars...

00:11:55.948 --> 00:11:57.883
...a lot of chemicals
were manufactured...

00:11:57.883 --> 00:12:00.351
...for use in explosives
and poison gas.

00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:02.555
But at war's end...

00:12:02.555 --> 00:12:04.690
...all that becomes
nothing but a waste.

00:12:04.690 --> 00:12:08.126
You can't tear down the
factories afterwards, either.

00:12:09.128 --> 00:12:11.030
So, the surplus
poisonous gas...

00:12:11.030 --> 00:12:14.333
...was used as insecticide
in the fields.

00:12:14.333 --> 00:12:16.635
The nitrogen and materials
for the explosives...

00:12:16.635 --> 00:12:19.105
...were called
chemical fertilizers...

00:12:19.105 --> 00:12:21.574
...and were disposed of
in farmers' fields.

00:12:21.574 --> 00:12:21.774
Chemical fertilizer

00:12:21.774 --> 00:12:22.975
Chemical fertilizer

00:12:22.975 --> 00:12:25.307
As for nuclear waste
material from uranium...

00:12:25.544 --> 00:12:27.947
...it was deemed to be
depleted uranium...

00:12:27.947 --> 00:12:31.178
...and disposed of in
other countries.

00:12:35.721 --> 00:12:36.881
No.

00:12:37.456 --> 00:12:40.025
Modern civilization
is a pile of garbage.

00:12:40.025 --> 00:12:43.062
It produces excessive amounts
of things we don't even need.

00:12:43.062 --> 00:12:45.464
And troubled by how to
dispose of it...

00:12:45.464 --> 00:12:50.094
...the world collapses under the
weight of the garbage it produced.

00:13:41.353 --> 00:13:44.049
Are you thinking
about Chris again?

00:13:46.091 --> 00:13:49.424
You've got to leave
Chris alone for awhile.

00:13:50.963 --> 00:13:52.521
Is that it?

00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:56.302
You dragged me around all day...

00:13:56.302 --> 00:13:58.770
...just because you wanted
to tell me that?

00:14:11.884 --> 00:14:13.579
Are you sure about that?

00:14:13.919 --> 00:14:14.510
Huh?

00:14:15.254 --> 00:14:17.279
Just giving up so easily?

00:14:18.424 --> 00:14:19.721
Of course not.

00:14:19.925 --> 00:14:22.261
But that is the fate of
modern civilization.

00:14:22.261 --> 00:14:24.752
No, I'm talking about Kevin.

00:14:24.964 --> 00:14:25.692
Kevin?

00:14:26.065 --> 00:14:29.635
Anyone should be allowed to
fall in love with anyone, right?

00:14:29.635 --> 00:14:32.195
This is the land of freedom.

00:14:36.976 --> 00:14:40.279
Kevin said he didn't have
a problem with my condition.

00:14:40.279 --> 00:14:42.213
That he didn't mind that
I couldn't have children.

00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:46.718
But I couldn't abandon it.

00:14:47.720 --> 00:14:50.222
I couldn't give up the job...

00:14:50.222 --> 00:14:52.458
...of fighting against this
evil modern civilization...

00:14:52.458 --> 00:14:54.050
...that did this to my body.

00:15:04.503 --> 00:15:05.437
Does it bother you?

00:15:05.437 --> 00:15:06.131
Huh?

00:15:07.273 --> 00:15:09.074
Uh, no. Not at all.

00:15:09.074 --> 00:15:10.009
Sorry.

00:15:10.009 --> 00:15:12.544
I have to deal with it now,
or it'll just accumulate.

00:15:12.544 --> 00:15:13.979
There's underwear in there, too.

00:15:13.979 --> 00:15:15.047
Huh?

00:15:15.047 --> 00:15:17.082
If you want, I can get you a pair.

00:15:17.082 --> 00:15:19.018
Hey, stupid. What are you saying?

00:15:19.018 --> 00:15:22.385
You wouldn't want some, would you?
Yucky girl's stuff.

00:15:23.022 --> 00:15:24.590
Maybe I'll take one.

00:15:24.590 --> 00:15:25.989
Come on!

00:15:27.359 --> 00:15:30.296
Well, things sure seem lively here.

00:15:30.296 --> 00:15:32.059
Oh, you're awake.

00:15:32.398 --> 00:15:35.067
You've got a guest.

00:15:35.067 --> 00:15:36.702
Uh, nice to meet you.

00:15:36.702 --> 00:15:38.033
I'm Oshima.

00:15:45.344 --> 00:15:47.437
Welcome.

00:15:48.881 --> 00:15:51.817
Oh, that's so embarrassing.

00:15:51.817 --> 00:15:53.085
I'm taking it!

00:15:53.085 --> 00:15:54.386
Hey, that's mine!

00:15:54.386 --> 00:15:55.287
Kimitoshi!

00:15:55.287 --> 00:15:57.222
Shut up, you little pig.

00:15:57.222 --> 00:15:59.425
On sale for seventy-eight yen
per one hundred grams.

00:15:59.425 --> 00:16:01.052
Look, you!

00:16:02.561 --> 00:16:05.860
I can't handle it any more.
My family's so lame.

00:16:06.398 --> 00:16:08.167
That's not true.

00:16:08.167 --> 00:16:10.601
It's a nice, warm home.

00:16:17.242 --> 00:16:19.767
Oh, we're simply noisy.

00:16:20.479 --> 00:16:21.776
I'm envious.

00:16:22.081 --> 00:16:24.777
My home is strangely silent.

00:16:26.018 --> 00:16:27.542
Oshima...

00:16:28.887 --> 00:16:30.089
Actually...

00:16:30.089 --> 00:16:34.025
...it's not that difficult to solve
the problems of this planet.

00:16:34.226 --> 00:16:34.749
Huh?

00:16:35.594 --> 00:16:37.396
If only each of us...

00:16:37.396 --> 00:16:42.390
...could truly understand what we
need from the bottom of our hearts.

00:16:43.268 --> 00:16:45.259
That's all that's necessary?

00:16:45.404 --> 00:16:47.497
Then why hasn't it worked?

00:16:47.606 --> 00:16:50.676
We're surrounded by convenient
things that run on gas and electricity...

00:16:50.676 --> 00:16:53.479
...we indulge ourselves in luxury
and use cell phones and such.

00:16:53.479 --> 00:16:55.314
Think we could give up
a life like that?

00:16:55.314 --> 00:16:55.871
Huh?

00:17:01.553 --> 00:17:02.955
A little bit.

00:17:02.955 --> 00:17:05.219
- Then, what about your family?
- Huh?

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:10.394
Well, um...

00:17:10.829 --> 00:17:12.364
How about your boyfriend?

00:17:12.364 --> 00:17:13.058
Boyfriend?

00:17:16.602 --> 00:17:17.432
No.

00:17:17.703 --> 00:17:19.933
No way. Not him.

00:17:22.007 --> 00:17:25.204
You should believe in him a little
more. He is your boyfriend, right?

00:17:25.344 --> 00:17:26.504
Yeah, but...

00:17:27.146 --> 00:17:29.581
Do you know why
they can't give it up?

00:17:29.581 --> 00:17:29.979
Huh?

00:17:31.717 --> 00:17:33.150
Well, um...

00:17:36.188 --> 00:17:37.256
It's because of fear.

00:17:37.256 --> 00:17:37.950
Fear?

00:17:38.424 --> 00:17:39.220
Of what?

00:17:40.225 --> 00:17:41.860
Once you start something...

00:17:41.860 --> 00:17:43.228
...once you acquire something...

00:17:43.228 --> 00:17:45.531
...there's a fear of giving it up.

00:17:45.531 --> 00:17:48.329
What is important in life becomes
confusing.

00:17:49.501 --> 00:17:52.902
That's why people have to
become aware as soon as possible.

00:18:27.539 --> 00:18:30.201
The raw gluten is
a specialty here.

00:18:33.879 --> 00:18:38.248
At least share the taste
of the delicacy with Chris.

00:18:42.287 --> 00:18:45.188
Chris says he can't eat anymore.

00:18:56.268 --> 00:18:59.471
Before all these dishes were
served in front of you...

00:18:59.471 --> 00:19:03.965
...the work of hundreds of
nameless cooks went into them.

00:19:04.543 --> 00:19:07.740
That's what human nature
is all about.

00:19:08.147 --> 00:19:09.248
In a sense...

00:19:09.248 --> 00:19:14.652
...that one taste may be heavier
than the life of one human being.

00:19:30.235 --> 00:19:32.669
I'll be off now, dear.

00:19:33.605 --> 00:19:35.641
Are you off to work?

00:19:35.641 --> 00:19:38.201
I'm on a nightshift tonight.

00:19:38.310 --> 00:19:41.079
That means I won't be home
until the morning...

00:19:41.079 --> 00:19:42.714
...so feel free to spend the night
if you want.

00:19:42.714 --> 00:19:44.616
Dad! What're you saying?!

00:19:44.616 --> 00:19:46.518
Well, enjoy yourself.

00:19:46.518 --> 00:19:47.985
See ya!

00:19:48.420 --> 00:19:50.854
Show some consideration
for Oshima!

00:19:52.324 --> 00:19:53.959
So, Oshima...

00:19:53.959 --> 00:19:54.482
Huh?

00:19:55.394 --> 00:19:57.362
If he's going to spend the night...

00:19:57.362 --> 00:19:59.598
...where am I going to sleep?

00:19:59.598 --> 00:20:02.431
Don't worry.
He'll sleep in Dad's bed.

00:20:03.101 --> 00:20:04.303
Oh, no!

00:20:04.303 --> 00:20:06.703
I wasn't suggesting you should
spend the night.

00:20:08.840 --> 00:20:09.704
I...

00:20:12.077 --> 00:20:12.736
Sorry.

00:20:14.046 --> 00:20:15.479
Hello?

00:20:15.847 --> 00:20:16.677
Juna?!

00:20:17.716 --> 00:20:18.546
Tokio!

00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:22.721
Thank goodness.

00:20:22.721 --> 00:20:24.313
I got through.

00:20:25.624 --> 00:20:26.558
Juna!

00:20:26.558 --> 00:20:28.549
Where the heck are you?!

00:20:29.061 --> 00:20:29.584
Huh?!

00:20:30.028 --> 00:20:31.461
New York?!

00:20:32.431 --> 00:20:33.332
Juna!

00:20:33.332 --> 00:20:34.833
What are you doing?!

00:20:34.833 --> 00:20:37.669
If you don't cut it out, I won't be
able to keep my mouth shut!

00:20:37.669 --> 00:20:40.069
You better apologize to Oshima!

00:20:41.807 --> 00:20:42.501
Hello?

00:20:42.841 --> 00:20:44.376
Hey, Tokio!

00:20:44.376 --> 00:20:46.445
What's going on, anyway?

00:20:46.445 --> 00:20:48.680
Why is Sayuri there?!

00:20:48.680 --> 00:20:49.848
Uh, well, uh...

00:20:49.848 --> 00:20:51.550
It's a long story.

00:20:51.550 --> 00:20:54.052
I'm the one who called you!

00:20:54.052 --> 00:20:56.388
So, why do I have to have
Sayuri chew me out?!

00:20:56.388 --> 00:20:58.056
Yeah, I know...

00:20:58.056 --> 00:21:01.457
...but if you don't get
in touch or anything...

00:21:04.129 --> 00:21:04.925
Tokio?!

00:21:05.030 --> 00:21:06.258
Tokio?!

00:21:12.804 --> 00:21:13.438
Huh?

00:21:13.438 --> 00:21:14.803
Why was I cut off?

00:21:16.308 --> 00:21:18.043
Why would there be
a blackout now?

00:21:18.043 --> 00:21:19.811
A ghost's going to come out!

00:21:19.811 --> 00:21:21.176
Stop it!

00:21:38.196 --> 00:21:39.026
What the...?!

00:21:41.099 --> 00:21:41.929
It's begun.

00:21:42.768 --> 00:21:43.962
It's begun?

00:21:44.670 --> 00:21:45.904
Tokio! Tokio!

00:21:45.904 --> 00:21:47.098
Earth Maiden Arjuna

00:21:48.407 --> 00:21:52.744
Ikanakucha fukai kurayami ni

00:21:52.744 --> 00:21:55.814
Mayoikonda kare wo

00:21:55.814 --> 00:22:00.085
Daremo tasukete kurenai

00:22:00.085 --> 00:22:04.756
Atashi nara itoshisa dake de

00:22:04.756 --> 00:22:07.759
Donna basho e demo

00:22:07.759 --> 00:22:12.030
Mayowanai de hashitte yukeru

00:22:12.030 --> 00:22:16.735
Dakara ooki na koe de

00:22:16.735 --> 00:22:23.809
Nandomo atashi no namae wo yonde

00:22:23.809 --> 00:22:26.778
Dareyori hayaku

00:22:26.778 --> 00:22:32.784
Tadoritsuite miseru yo

00:22:32.784 --> 00:22:44.560
Kiminomoto e

00:22:45.597 --> 00:22:49.761
There was a time when there
was no garbage on this planet.

00:22:50.969 --> 00:22:55.804
A time when there was nothing
that they didn't need.

00:23:00.912 --> 00:23:02.379
Nothing...

00:23:03.582 --> 00:23:05.015
...no one...

00:23:05.951 --> 00:23:07.282
...at all.

00:23:21.633 --> 00:23:24.436
One quiet autumn night...

00:23:24.436 --> 00:23:27.701
...a nation died.

00:23:31.009 --> 00:23:32.909
W-We've got to get out of here!

00:23:33.879 --> 00:23:34.641
I'm sorry.

00:23:35.280 --> 00:23:36.348
What?

00:23:36.348 --> 00:23:38.339
Why are you apologizing?

00:23:41.253 --> 00:23:42.015
I'm really sorry.

00:23:44.289 --> 00:23:46.757
It's hot! It's hot!

00:23:47.325 --> 00:23:50.226
Ashura is materializing!

00:23:50.996 --> 00:23:51.655
Faster!

00:23:51.863 --> 00:23:52.989
Faster!

00:23:54.399 --> 00:23:55.388
You fool.

00:23:56.668 --> 00:23:59.762
Are you going to go and
destroy the world with anger?

00:24:00.672 --> 00:24:01.468
Chris!

00:24:01.840 --> 00:24:02.602
Chris!

00:24:03.875 --> 00:24:04.534
Juna!

00:24:04.776 --> 00:24:05.610
Juna!

00:24:05.610 --> 00:24:07.009
Sayuri! Sayuri!

00:24:07.312 --> 00:24:08.780
Get it together! Sayuri!

00:24:08.780 --> 00:24:10.372
Tokio...

00:24:11.383 --> 00:24:13.681
Can we still not see the way?

00:24:14.085 --> 00:24:16.955
Episode 12: The Death of a Nation

00:24:16.955 --> 00:24:22.325
Episode 13: The Here and Now
